      "run": 2,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "I find myself in a small, confined galley where salt has invaded every corner, leaving a gritty texture underfoot and an overpowering taste in the air. Within this space, amidst the chaos of disarray, I stumbled upon a kettle and decided to claim it as my own, considering its potential use in purifying water or boiling something edible.\n\nThe journey led me northwards from the discomforting galley into a store that seemed to hold more potential for sustenance. The air was heavy with the scent of paraffin, perhaps from lanterns or other containers that once lined the now mostly empty shelves. This new environment, while still far from inviting, hinted at prior activity and the presence of others who had once prepared or stored necessary supplies.\n\nIn the store, I noticed a coil of rope neglected on the floor\u2014a treasure in its own right, particularly if exploration or escape required any form of climbing or securing. With practicality in mind, I grasped the rope, adding it to my meager collection of salvaged items. The workshop lies ahead, beckoning with promises of more",
